#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Bring Monolith, your apps and your tools up to date.

This is `monolith update`, which `update` and `upgrade` on their own run too.
`monolith update APP...` goes to the catalog instead, so it never reaches this
script.

Each step runs on its own, with no terminal attached, and one failing doesn't
stop the rest. Their full output goes to ~/.local/state/monolith/update/. On a
terminal the update plays the Sunrise: Monolith's mark rises out of the ground
and the sun comes up behind it as the steps finish. Piped output, NO_COLOR and
the Linux console get plain lines, and MONOLITH_MOTION=0 keeps the picture
still. A run that gets through every step is recorded for the login reminder,
`monolith status` and the greeting.

Tests point these at stand-ins: MONOLITH_OS_RELEASE, MONOLITH_LOGOS,
MONOLITH_OSTREE_BOOTED, FLATPAK_USER_DIR, FLATPAK_SYSTEM_DIR, and
MONOLITH_UPDATE_POLL, the seconds between checks while waiting.
"""
